          "input": "const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /tmp/llame-semantic-run-checkpoints-issue.md\\n+## Outcome\\n+\\n+After worker death and queue redelivery, a non-terminal Run continues from its last committed semantic boundary. It does not restart the whole tool loop, re-execute a settled tool call, or silently treat an ambiguous external effect as safe to retry.\\n+\\n+## Scope\\n+\\n+- Define durable model-step and tool-invocation identity owned by llame rather than provider-generated call IDs alone.\\n+- Persist tool intent before dispatch and persist its normalized result or error before advancing to the next model step.\\n+- Reconstruct provider context from committed steps and reuse settled tool results after recovery.\\n+- Distinguish work not dispatched, work known settled, and work that may have executed but has no durable result (`outcome_unknown`).\\n+- Automatically repeat only executions whose read-only or idempotency/deduplication contract is independently enforceable. Stop for reconciliation otherwise.\\n+- Fence progress and terminal settlement against stale workers after lease loss or queue redelivery.\\n+- Treat an interrupted provider stream as an interrupted attempt followed by a fresh inference from the last committed semantic boundary; do not claim token-level continuation.\\n+- Preserve any durable partial assistant output without presenting duplicated or contradictory output after recovery.\\n+\\n+## Acceptance\\n+\\n+- [ ] A real worker-process kill before tool dispatch recovers without losing the committed model step.\\n+- [ ] A kill after tool dispatch but before result persistence records an ambiguous outcome and does not automatically repeat a non-idempotent effect.\\n+- [ ] A kill after result persistence reuses that result without invoking the tool again.\\n+- [ ] A kill during model streaming preserves the durable partial attempt and resumes with a fresh, coherent model step.\\n+- [ ] A stale worker cannot append pr